      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:13ad3691c02d649360993afa371c4f30f63e574cced6673e6a9f762481153958",
      "text": "Collector handoff needs both ownership control and a recoverable processing position. Leases can leave an expired owner running, so protected writes need resource-enforced fencing. Graceful release must follow completion of guarded work. Recovery should make processing durable before reporting completion and tolerate replay through idempotency. Salesforce subscriptions resume from stored replay positions within the retention window. Administrative stopping of a managed subscription deletes its committed position. Redis-backed fencing also needs scrutiny because asynchronous failover can lose token increments.",
